hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1449","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Allah said"""
"1450","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, They say Al-Karm (the generous) ""1451"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""
"1451","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he said: ""Let none of you say, 'Feed your Lord,' 'Wash your Lord,' or 'Give drink to your Lord.' Rather, let him say, 'My master,' 'My patron.' And let none of you say, 'My male slave,' 'My female slave,' but let him say, 'My young man,' 'My young woman,' and 'My boy.'""
1452"""
"1452","Narrated 'Aishah: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""None of you should say, 'My soul has become khabuthat (foul, wicked),' but he should say, 'My soul has become laqisat (uneasy, distressed).'"""
"1453","Narrated Sal:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \None of you should say Khabuthat Nafsi but he is recommended to say 'Laqisat \nNafsi (See Hadith No. 202)"""""""
